      "content": "Coding agents frequently break down when faced with dependency updates released after their training cutoff. Instead of navigating modern breaking changes, the model repeatedly attempts deprecated API signatures, burns through context tokens, and loops on compiler errors.\n\nStalemap tackles this failure mode by comparing installed package versions against the model knowledge base. It extracts type declaration diffs, upgrade notes, and documentation changes, then injects a ranked summary directly into project context files and MCP tool hooks. It couples this with automated compiler guards to catch altered configuration keys and renamed APIs before edits land.\n\nIn controlled benchmark evaluations across 66 post-cutoff package updates, providing targeted API diffs improved coding agent pass rates by over 20 points compared to unassisted sessions. Initial edits containing stale API usage dropped from 27 percent down to 11 percent.\n\nThis confirms an essential lesson in agentic infrastructure: precise context curation beats asking the model to blindly discover breaking changes through raw error cycles."
