      "image": null,
      "content": "A monolithic harness rarely works well across diverse agent tasks because a single prompt, tool configuration, and control loop cannot satisfy competing execution requirements.\n\nGoogle Cloud AI Research and UIUC introduced OO-Harness, an approach that applies object-oriented inheritance to agent engineering. Instead of maintaining a sprawling global prompt or rigid conditional trees, an evolution agent inspects execution traces and automatically subclasses existing harnesses. Common setup and tooling remain in parent classes, while specialized child classes override only the prompts, heuristics, or tools that require domain-specific adjustments.\n\nAt runtime, a trained router classifies the incoming task and delegates it down the class hierarchy to the most suitable subclass. On benchmarks spanning workspace tasks and complex tool use, this modular architecture yielded up to fifteen points of absolute improvement over standard baselines.\n\nClean software architecture patterns like inheritance often solve agent steering problems better than raw prompt tweaking."
