      "content": "Relying on general-purpose large language models as judges for evaluation suites is often needlessly slow and expensive. Dedicated decision models like TypeSafe Jev, Perplexity Decider, and OpenAI Decisions API offer a much faster, cost-effective alternative for automated classification tasks.\n\nThe default classification threshold of 0.50 is rarely optimal for production evaluation pipelines. When benchmarking these models on realistic agent traces, tuning the classification threshold directly against your precision and recall requirements yields massive performance improvements without changing the underlying model weights.\n\nModel calibration is equally critical when treating outputs as confidence metrics. Uncalibrated scores can skew routing logic and alert triggers, whereas calibrated probabilities allow engineers to set rigorous risk budgets when triaging failing traces.\n\nSwitching to specialized decision models and properly tuning their thresholds can dramatically lower evaluation latency while preserving judging accuracy.\n\nStop paying frontier model prices for basic binary classification."
